{"key": "decision-used-tmpl-variable-fallback-chain-covering-all-platfor", "type": "decision", "content": "used _TMPL variable + || fallback chain covering all platform paths (project-local .claude/.opencode/.cortex/skills/, Gemini project-root skills/, global ~/.config/opencode and ~/.snowflake/cortex) \u2014 first successful cat wins. Updated OpenCode and Gemini installers to copy references/ subdirectory alongside SKILL.md. Cortex already uses cp -r.\ngit add plugins/lavra/commands/lavra-work-ralph.md plugins/lavra/commands/lavra-work-teams.md plugins/lavra/skills/lavra-work-multi/SKILL.md installers/install-opencode.sh installers/install-gemini.sh\ngit commit -m \"fix(lavra-ceh.7): platform-agnostic subagent template path with fallback chain for all install locations\ngit push", "source": "user", "tags": ["decision", "fix", "config"], "ts": 1776201168, "bead": "lavra-ceh.7"}
{"key": "decision-path-rewriting-belongs-in-converters-not-runtime-each-pl", "type": "decision", "content": "path rewriting belongs in converters not runtime \u2014 each platform's generated files get a single correct hardcoded path baked in at install time. Pattern: add .replace() in both convertCommands() and convertSkills() of each converter script.\ngit add plugins/lavra/commands/lavra-work-ralph.md plugins/lavra/commands/lavra-work-teams.md plugins/lavra/skills/lavra-work-multi/SKILL.md scripts/convert-opencode.ts scripts/convert-gemini.ts scripts/convert-cortex.ts plugins/lavra/opencode/ plugins/lavra/gemini/ plugins/lavra/cortex/\ngit commit -m \"refactor(lavra-ceh.8): rewrite .claude/skills/ paths in converters, remove runtime fallback chain\ngit push", "source": "user", "tags": ["decision", "pattern"], "ts": 1776203498, "bead": "lavra-ceh.8"}
{"key": "investigation-decision-intensity-caveman-lite-only-caveman-full-risks", "type": "investigation", "content": "DECISION: Intensity = caveman-lite only. Caveman-full risks ambiguity in multi-step agent flows.\nDECISION: Safety sections (guardrails, irreversible ops, security warnings) preserved as full prose -- follow caveman auto-clarity rule.\nDECISION: Examples -- compress framing prose, preserve literal example content unchanged.\nDECISION: LLM-based script (not regex) for compression -- context-aware, handles edge cases.\nDECISION: compress-prose.ts in scripts/, bun runtime, consistent with convert-opencode.ts pattern.\nDECISION: New file workflow = style guide at .claude/rules/prose-style.md + pre-release-check.sh integration.\nFACT: Caveman skill at /Users/rbm/dotfiles/claude/plugins/marketplaces/caveman -- not in lavra repo.\nVerbosity sources -- articles, hedging phrases (Make sure to, Note that, Be sure to), defensive guards, narrative role sections", "source": "user", "tags": ["investigation", "security", "ui", "pattern", "decision"], "ts": 1776209691, "bead": "lavra-ziy"}
{"key": "decision-caveman-skill-is-mit-licensed-julius-brussee-2026-do-not", "type": "decision", "content": "Caveman skill is MIT licensed (Julius Brussee, 2026). Do NOT bundle into Lavra -- reference only to avoid maintenance burden. Installer should recommend 'npx lavra@caveman' or equivalent during setup", "source": "user", "tags": ["decision", "ui"], "ts": 1776209947, "bead": "lavra-ziy"}
