{"key": "investigation-pattern-existing-bun-scripts-use-readfilesafe-writefilesa", "type": "investigation", "content": "PATTERN: Existing bun scripts use readFileSafe()/writeFileSafe() from scripts/shared/security.ts. File permissions must be 0o644. No script in repo currently calls Claude API -- compress-prose.ts is first.\nconvert-opencode.ts uses Promise.all for parallel processing. For API rate limits, prefer sequential on first version.\nPATTERN: pre-release-check.sh adds checks with check() helper. Runs (cd scripts && bun install --frozen-lockfile && bun run X.ts). Must add SYNC comment pointing to .github/workflows/test-installation.yml.\nFACT: Post-install messaging in installers/install-claude.sh uses 2-space indent, blank lines. Appears after 'Done.' Delegates from bin/install.js via shell exec", "source": "user", "tags": ["investigation", "api", "security", "test", "pattern"], "ts": 1776210240, "bead": "lavra-ziy.2"}
{"key": "decision-compress-prose-ts-shells-out-to-agent-cli-claude-p-tmpf", "type": "decision", "content": "compress-prose.ts shells out to agent CLI (claude -p \\\"@tmpfile\\\") instead of calling Anthropic SDK. No SDK dependency, no API key config -- uses user's existing auth. Agent configurable via .lavra/config/compress.json or --agent flag. Default: claude", "source": "user", "tags": ["decision", "api", "auth", "config"], "ts": 1776210552, "bead": "lavra-ziy.2"}
{"key": "investigation-claude-p-filepath-is-undocumented-behavior-use-stdin-pipi", "type": "investigation", "content": "claude -p @filepath is undocumented behavior. Use stdin piping instead: Bun.spawn(['claude', '-p', '--output-format', 'text', '/dev/stdin'], {stdin: 'pipe'}). Write prompt, proc.stdin.write(prompt), proc.stdin.end().\nPATTERN: Pre-process file before sending to LLM -- wrap preserve regions in <preserve verbatim='true'> tags. Strip tags from output. Regions: fenced code blocks, safety/warning sections, multi-step sequences, literal example content.\nPATTERN: Prompt structure for idempotency -- repeat output constraint at end (recency bias). 'If already compressed per rules, copy unchanged.' Keep full sentences rule prevents re-compression of already-compressed text.\nFACT: No existing Bun.spawn usage in scripts/ -- compress-prose.ts will be first. Bun.spawn preferred over child_process.exec (no 1MB buffer cap). Use try/finally for temp file cleanup (os.tmpdir() returns /var/folders/... on macOS)", "source": "user", "tags": ["investigation", "pattern", "constraint"], "ts": 1776211255, "bead": "lavra-ziy.2"}
{"key": "decision-ceo-review-major-pivot-drop-compress-prose-ts-automated", "type": "decision", "content": "CEO review -- MAJOR PIVOT. Drop compress-prose.ts automated script. Primary mechanism: authoring rules in .claude/rules/prose-style.md. Developers follow rules when writing/modifying files. No automation, no idempotency risk, no CLI invocation complexity.\nCEO review -- one-time manual agent pass to compress all 59+ existing files. Done once, committed. After that, style guide is the gate.\nCEO review -- add rg-based WARN check to pre-release-check.sh. Detects known filler phrases in modified files. WARN not FAIL. Add in Phase 1 alongside style guide", "source": "user", "tags": ["decision", "ui", "auth"], "ts": 1776211661, "bead": "lavra-ziy"}
{"key": "learned-decision-engineering-review-applied-10-recommendations-9", "type": "learned", "content": "DECISION: Engineering review applied. 10 recommendations, 9 applied, 1 skipped (generate-command audit -- Claude built-in, not Lavra-owned). Key changes: phase restructure 5\u21923 core phases, rg availability guard, CI sync deferred to after compression, caveman URL pinned, tiktoken \u2192 count_tokens API.\nEffective whole-file token reduction is ~10-18% (not 20-30%) because code blocks are 40-60% of file length and unchanged. 20-30% is prose-only. Distinguish these in communications.\nFACT: Caveman skill repo: https://github.com/JuliusBrussee/caveman (MIT, Julius Brussee). Verified URL for installer recommendation", "source": "user", "tags": ["learned", "api", "ui", "engine", "decision", "rest"], "ts": 1776212362, "bead": "lavra-ziy"}
