{"key": "learned-4fa8602f901b", "type": "learned", "content": "Action in AI agent operations refers to discrete executable steps, such as API calls or command executions, that require clear definitions of triggers, inputs, and expected outcomes. Proper action design includes validation, error handling, and logging to ensure reliability and traceability. Even from limited experience, encapsulating actions with modular interfaces improves reusability and debugging.", "source": "knowledge-cube", "tags": ["[\"complexity:low\"]", "auto_tagged", "debugging"], "ts": 1781120612, "bead": ""}
{"key": "learned-c0e7bee5d5de", "type": "learned", "content": "AI agents must decompose high-level goals into executable action sequences, selecting appropriate tools or APIs for each step. During execution, continuously monitor outcomes against expected results and capture execution metadata for debugging. Implement fallback strategies for common failure modes (timeouts, rate limits, invalid responses) and log sufficient context to enable retrospective analysis and policy improvement.", "source": "knowledge-cube", "tags": ["[\"pattern:recurring\"", "\"complexity:low\"]", "auto_tagged", "bugfix"], "ts": 1781120657, "bead": ""}
