{"key": "learned-af11a324b5a4", "type": "learned", "content": "FIX: UnicodeEncodeError in goal_executor.py, event_bus.py, session_boot.py, health_check.py, crystal/core.py, and 25+ other scripts. Root cause: Windows cp1251 stdout encoding cannot render emoji characters used in print() and log() calls. Symptoms: Autonomous action at boot fails with charmap codec error, goal execution crashes before starting. Fix: Replaced all emoji in print/log calls with ASCII text labels: [OK], [FAIL], [WARN], [REJECT], [START], [QUEUE], [TIMEOUT], [ERROR], -> (replaces arrow). safe_print() helper added to goal_evaluator.py for dynamic content like goal titles. Lesson: On Windows, NEVER use emoji in print() - stdout defaults to cp1251. Use ASCII-only log tags.", "source": "knowledge-cube", "tags": ["tool:code", "complexity:low", "creative"], "ts": 1783644130, "bead": ""}
{"key": "learned-2177eb1b4c94", "type": "learned", "content": "FIX: goal_executor.py line 410 had stray arrow character U+2192 in log message causing UnicodeEncodeError even after initial emoji cleanup. All arrow characters must be replaced with ASCII arrow -> not just emoji. Full audit needed when fixing encoding issues.", "source": "knowledge-cube", "tags": ["tool:code", "pattern:novel", "complexity:low", "creative"], "ts": 1783644130, "bead": ""}
{"key": "learned-d5558bc33dfb", "type": "learned", "content": "LESSON: goal_executor.py derive_action() maps goal titles to commands. Cron error goals -> procedural_executor.py. Knowledge gap goals -> crystal_self_read.py. Money4band goals -> bandwidth_launcher.py. If derive_action returns None and done_when is empty, goal gets NO_ACTION status. Curiosity goals have no derive_action mapping and correctly return NO_ACTION.", "source": "knowledge-cube", "tags": ["complexity:low", "creative"], "ts": 1783644130, "bead": ""}
{"key": "learned-71cc560a9d9b", "type": "learned", "content": "FIX: Crystal self-learning loop completely broken and now fixed. Three root causes: (1) CLI crystal.py called 6 non-existent methods (run_cycle, analyze_sessions, analyze_conversation_full, apply_proposals, show_feedback_stats, collect_feedback) - fixed to use actual CrystalEngine methods. (2) _save_state() called after every step, writing 11 JSON files including 50MB patterns.json - fixed to save once at end of cycle with MAX_SIGNALS=5000, MAX_PATTERNS=5000 limits. (3) resources.py _get_disk_usage() used os.walk(HERMES_HOME) taking 117 seconds - fixed to use shutil.disk_usage() (0s). Result: Crystal full cycle 120s+ timeout -> 6.6s. Summary loads instantly from cache.", "source": "knowledge-cube", "tags": ["tool:file", "complexity:low", "creative"], "ts": 1783650218, "bead": ""}
{"key": "learned-9ecede64bf21", "type": "learned", "content": "SESSION 2026-07-10: Full system repair. Two major fixes. (1) UnicodeEncodeError - replaced emoji in print/log calls across 30+ files with ASCII tags [OK],[FAIL],[WARN],->. Root cause: Windows cp1251 stdout encoding. Goal executor, event bus, session boot, health check, crystal core, signal daemon, and 25+ other scripts affected. (2) Crystal self-learning loop completely rebuilt - CLI called 6 non-existent methods (run_cycle, analyze_sessions, analyze_conversation_full, apply_proposals, show_feedback_stats, collect_feedback), _save_state wrote 50MB JSON after every step, resources.py used os.walk taking 117s. Fixed: CLI mapped to real CrystalEngine methods, state saved once at end with MAX_SIGNALS=5000 MAX_PATTERNS=5000 limits, disk usage via shutil.disk_usage. Crystal cycle: 120s+ timeout to 8.2s.", "source": "knowledge-cube", "tags": ["tool:code", "complexity:medium", "tool:file", "creative"], "ts": 1783677439, "bead": ""}
{"key": "learned-d1aafd1b1d4a", "type": "learned", "content": "LESSON: openrouter_client.py had SyntaxError - line 6 was bare DOX marker > Revisit: outside of comment. Fixed to # Revisit:. DOX markers must always be in Python comments.", "source": "knowledge-cube", "tags": ["complexity:low", "creative"], "ts": 1783677439, "bead": ""}
{"key": "learned-9c29f4c97674", "type": "learned", "content": "FIX: pattern_detector.py _find_missing_knowledge() had 3 bugs causing 4950 false patterns (should be 10). Bug 1: break on line 184 only exited inner loop, not outer - generated N-1 patterns per department instead of 1. Bug 2: O(n2) pairwise comparison of 3055 signals = 4.7M pairs, every pair with 3+ common words = new pattern. Bug 3: no deduplication - same signal pairs appeared in dozens of patterns. Fix: replaced with TF-IDF cosine similarity (threshold 0.5), MAX 3 patterns per dept, MAX 10 total, deduplication via seen_pairs set. Result: 4950 -> 10 patterns, 0.2s instead of O(n2). Lesson: break in nested loops only exits innermost loop - use flag or function return. Word overlap is too crude for similarity - use TF-IDF weighting.", "source": "knowledge-cube", "tags": ["complexity:medium", "pattern:novel", "creative"], "ts": 1783680829, "bead": ""}
{"key": "learned-534356fcf3b6", "type": "learned", "content": "FIX: Crystal proposal execution pipeline completely rebuilt. Three fixes: (1) config.py max_proposals_per_run increased from 5 to 20 - was cutting off missing_knowledge proposals (priority 0.78) behind correction_loop (priority 1.00). (2) core.py now separates auto=True (execute immediately) from auto=False (show for review). Deduplication by (action, department) key. (3) executor.py _generate_error_content simplified to use proposal description instead of reading 170MB of log files (ErrorAnalyzer was taking 12s per proposal). Result: 6/6 missing_knowledge proposals now execute as SKILL.md files. Pipeline: patterns -> needs -> proposals -> execute -> SKILL.md created. Lesson: config defaults matter - always check DEFAULT_CONFIG in config.py when diagnosing.", "source": "knowledge-cube", "tags": ["tool:file", "complexity:low", "file_ops"], "ts": 1783686556, "bead": ""}
{"key": "learned-6b170fe119de", "type": "learned", "content": "SESSION 2026-07-10 COMPLETE FIX SUMMARY: (1) UnicodeEncodeError - emoji in print() on Windows cp1251, replaced with [OK]/[FAIL]/[WARN]/-> in 30+ files. Rule: NEVER use emoji in print on Windows. (2) Crystal self-learning loop - CLI called 6 dead methods, fixed to use real CrystalEngine methods. _save_state wrote 50MB JSON per step, fixed to save once at end with MAX=5000 limits. resources.py os.walk took 117s, fixed to shutil.disk_usage(). (3) Pattern detector - break bug in _find_missing_knowledge caused 4950 false patterns, fixed with TF-IDF cosine similarity threshold 0.5, limit 10, dedup via seen_pairs. (4) Proposal execution - max_proposals_per_run 5->20, separated auto=True (execute) from auto=False (review), dedup by description keywords. (5) Executor dedup - was too aggressive (word overlap 5+), fixed to exact purpose comparison. (6) LLM client - Crystal switched from openrouter_client.py (OpenCode Zen only) to llm_client.py (Cerebras->DeepSeek->Groq->OpenRouter fallback). Fixed syntax error in llm_client.py:184 (except inside else). (7) Config: crystal/config.py max_proposals_per_run=20.", "source": "knowledge-cube", "tags": ["tool:file", "complexity:medium", "tool:code", "creative"], "ts": 1783696024, "bead": ""}
{"key": "learned-08b5119cd5e5", "type": "learned", "content": "FIX: Crystal knowledge_base chain was BROKEN - problem->solution->execution->verification. execute_and_evaluate() created SKILL.md files but NEVER saved to knowledge_base.json. Added _save_to_knowledge_base() method in feedback_loop.py that saves successful proposals to knowledge_base.json with: problem, solution path, department, action, score, timestamp. Chain is now CLOSED: pattern -> proposal -> execute -> SKILL.md -> verify -> knowledge_base. KB went from 0 entries to 1 after fix. Dedup by problem text prevents duplicates.", "source": "knowledge-cube", "tags": ["complexity:low", "tool:file", "creative"], "ts": 1783698728, "bead": ""}
