{"key": "learned-35bf63ba2d7c", "type": "learned", "content": "Testing for AI agents involves validating outputs against expected behaviors, using unit tests for atomic operations, integration tests for workflows, and end-to-end tests for user interactions. Include edge cases, error handling, and ensure the agent's responses align with defined safety and quality standards. Regular test suites help maintain reliability during updates.", "source": "knowledge-cube", "tags": ["pattern:recurring", "complexity:low", "design"], "ts": 1784407242, "bead": ""}
{"key": "learned-403706d025d2", "type": "learned", "content": "Automation for AI agents means codifying repetitive workflows as reusable scripts or state machines that can be triggered by events, schedules, or API calls. Use idempotent operations and explicit error handling so retries are safe, and emit structured logs for observability. Integrate with external systems via authenticated APIs or message queues, and version-control automation definitions to enable rollback and audit.", "source": "knowledge-cube", "tags": ["complexity:low", "devops"], "ts": 1784407350, "bead": ""}
{"key": "learned-5a562346f04d", "type": "learned", "content": "Documentation serves as an external knowledge base that AI agents must maintain for consistent and autonomous operations. Use structured formats like Markdown or JSON with clear metadata to enable efficient parsing and retrieval. Documentation should cover system architecture, API endpoints, error handling, and decision-making processes to reduce dependency on real-time human input.", "source": "knowledge-cube", "tags": ["complexity:low", "data"], "ts": 1784407368, "bead": ""}
{"key": "learned-e01900969e8c", "type": "learned", "content": "Automation for AI agents involves designing workflows to execute repetitive, rule-based tasks with minimal human intervention, such as data processing or system monitoring. It ensures consistency, reduces operational overhead, and allows the agent to focus on complex decision-making. Effective automation requires clear task definition, error-handling protocols, and integration with existing tools and APIs.", "source": "knowledge-cube", "tags": ["complexity:low", "design"], "ts": 1784408403, "bead": ""}
{"key": "learned-1bbd2c2ddc9f", "type": "learned", "content": "Automation enables AI agents to execute repetitive tasks without human intervention by defining workflows, triggers, and error handling. Agents should use idempotent operations, state persistence, and observability to ensure reliability. Prioritize automating high-frequency, low-complexity tasks first to maximize ROI.", "source": "knowledge-cube", "tags": ["complexity:low", "pattern:novel"], "ts": 1784409412, "bead": ""}
