{"key": "learned-2aa1131ab5d5", "type": "learned", "content": "AI agents must maintain structured, version-controlled records of all decisions, tool invocations, and error resolutions for auditability and debugging. They should automatically generate and update user-facing documentation (API specs, runbooks, architecture diagrams) as part of task completion. Internal knowledge bases require continuous synchronization with executed workflows to prevent drift and enable future agent instances to inherit operational context.", "source": "knowledge-cube", "tags": ["complexity:low", "coding"], "ts": 1785495391, "bead": ""}
{"key": "learned-ec199fe54420", "type": "learned", "content": "Automation enables AI agents to execute repetitive or complex workflows autonomously by integrating with APIs, scripts, and scheduling systems. Agents should define clear triggers, handle errors with retries, and log outcomes for observability. Prioritize idempotent operations to safely retry failed steps.", "source": "knowledge-cube", "tags": ["complexity:low"], "ts": 1785507338, "bead": ""}
{"key": "decision-a43abe2cd010", "type": "decision", "content": "Documentation for AI agents must be machine-readable, versioned, and linked to executable code or workflows. Agents should automatically generate and update docs from source code, API specs, and decision logs using structured formats like OpenAPI or Markdown with frontmatter. Prioritize searchable, context-aware retrieval so agents can inject relevant docs into prompts during planning or debugging. Treat documentation as a first-class artifact in CI/CD pipelines to ensure consistency and freshness.", "source": "knowledge-cube", "tags": ["pattern:novel", "tool:code", "complexity:low", "coding"], "ts": 1785511622, "bead": ""}
{"key": "learned-cbd12d018acc", "type": "learned", "content": "Automation enables AI agents to execute repetitive or multi-step tasks without continuous human intervention by orchestrating APIs, scripts, and workflows. Agents should define clear triggers, idempotent actions, and error-handling retries to ensure reliability. Monitoring execution logs and performance metrics allows iterative improvement of automated processes.", "source": "knowledge-cube", "tags": ["complexity:low", "system"], "ts": 1785512788, "bead": ""}
{"key": "decision-f587d358ee68", "type": "decision", "content": "AI agents should maintain structured, version-controlled documentation of their capabilities, decision logic, and integration points to enable reproducibility and debugging. Automated documentation generation from code and runtime logs reduces manual overhead and ensures accuracy. Agents must parse external documentation (APIs, schemas) to adapt to new tools without human intervention. Regular audits of documentation completeness prevent knowledge drift in long-running deployments.", "source": "knowledge-cube", "tags": ["pattern:novel", "tool:code", "complexity:low", "coding"], "ts": 1785513893, "bead": ""}
